---
description: Use the platformio MCP tools (not shell `pio`) to build, flash, monitor, test, and debug firmware in this PlatformIO project.
globs: ["platformio.ini", "src/**/*.cpp", "src/**/*.c", "src/**/*.ino", "lib/**", "test/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- Build with `pio_build`; fix the returned `errors` (file, line, column) before anything else.
- Flash with `pio_flash_and_verify(expect="<healthy boot line>")` and act on `verdict`: `fail` comes with decoded frames, `timeout` means check port/baud.
- On any `Guru Meditation`, `Backtrace:`, or `HardFault` output, call `pio_decode_backtrace` and fix the first frame in project code.
- Stop serial sessions (`pio_monitor_stop`) before flashing.
- Add libraries with `pio_pkg_install`, which edits `platformio.ini` itself.
- Above 90% flash, run `pio_size_report` before adding features.
- Upload cannot open the port? Read `port_diagnosis` or call `pio_port_diagnose`; pass `stop_open_sessions=true` when our own session holds it.
- ESP32 flash looks fine but the device misbehaves: `pio_partition_table(read_device=true)`; after a crash with no serial dump, `pio_coredump`.
- Suspected leak or stack overflow: `pio_memory_watch` on the monitor session; add the `instrumentation_hint` snippet if nothing is recognized.
- Library conflicts or odd LDF behaviour: `pio_deps_check(build=true)`.
- Need breakpoints, not prints: `pio_debug_start` then `pio_debug_cmd`; stop the session before flashing.
